          <change when="2023-01-30T09:43:29-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/lgericke98">Submit - The supposed Ἡ of Ἡρακλέους in l. 10 is a π: other than in the case of the ‘chair-shaped’ etas in the same line, the left vertical stroke of this letter does not extend beyond the horizontal stroke. The restoration I suggest, τῆς λαμπροτάτης π[όλεως τῶν Ἀλεξανδρέων], appears in several second and third-century texts, e.g. Chr. Wilck. 428.</change>
          <change when="2023-01-30T09:35:24-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/lgericke98">Commit - The supposed Ἡ of Ἡρακλέους in l. 10 is a π; other than in the case of the ‘chair-shaped’ etas in the same line, the left vertical stroke of this letter does not extend beyond the horizontal stroke. τῆς λαμπροτάτης πόλεως τῶν Ἀλεξανδρέων appears in several second- and third-century texts such as P. Ryl. II 77 or Chr. Wilck. 428.</change>
